2026-11-12T04:24:46.3811140Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3840020Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3856370Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3858770Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3863100Z 
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3889630Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3892640Z 
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3894410Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3897820Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3901390Z 
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3911000Z If you would like to
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3920910Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3929500Z 
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3930660Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-12T04:24:46.3931180Z   $ sh ./install-nix
